Also the document.body child: wrap is a child of document.body — DOM parent-child references! In jsdom (and real browsers), a parent element holds references to its children. While wrap is a child of body, it won't be collected! Have to `wrap.remove()` / `document.body.removeChild(wrap)` before gc — the reproduction steps do exactly `wrap.remove()` after destroy. In real browsers, parent→child strong references exist (children array). So: after destroy, remove wrap from body, then gc.

